WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.520
"The Suicide Squad" is an&nbsp;
awesome, scary, hilarious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.160
badass, and ultimately heartwarming movie.&nbsp;
It's also a pretty straightforward story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.760
one whose loose ends get wrapped up&nbsp;
pretty thoroughly. Well, most of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.920
loose ends. Here are some of the biggest&nbsp;
unanswered questions in "The Suicide Squad."

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.240
The first action scene of the movie sees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.160
part of Task Force X land in the&nbsp;
water and set up for a beach assault.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.240
Blackguard walks out first and reveals&nbsp;
that he sold everyone out to the hostiles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.800
completely blowing everyone's cover and plan.&nbsp;
He then promptly gets his face blown off for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.040
his troubles and kicks off a firefight&nbsp;
that kills almost everyone on the beach.&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.280
This raises the first unanswered question of the&nbsp;
movie: How could he have possibly reached them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.480
while locked up? He's in a heavy security prison,&nbsp;
likely being monitored for much of the day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.880
How did he find his way around this, especially&nbsp;
in the short amount of time between getting his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.520
assignment and deployment, and contacting&nbsp;
the soldiers in Corto Maltese? Seeing as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.040
he's the first death of the movie, it's&nbsp;
unlikely we'll ever get the true story.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.360
This goes hand in hand with the question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.880
of how Blackguard betrayed everyone.&nbsp;
Though she's an expert at appearances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.120
Amanda Waller doesn't know everything about&nbsp;
everybody. She was, after all, completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.960
blindsided by Bloodsport's fear of rats —  
 
"I'm not shaking the rat's hand."
 &nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.720
— and seemingly didn't know that Blackguard&nbsp;
was going to blow everyone's cover immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.448
But it's hard not to wonder if she saw this&nbsp;
group, which she noted was a diversion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.448 --> 00:01:24.000
as even more disposable than the&nbsp;
average Task Force X operation.&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.960
This is a pretty pathetic group of heroes. Weasel&nbsp;
drowns almost immediately, but it's hard to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.920
what Weasel could have contributed under the best&nbsp;
of circumstances. Harley is a fan favorite, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.920
"audience popularity" doesn't make up for the fact&nbsp;
that she doesn't have many skills that would help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:44.000
in a firefight -- and she survived largely by dumb&nbsp;
luck. TDK is particularly pathetic, only using his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.560
detachable arms to lightly slap his opponents.
Characters occasionally remark that they didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.800
pick the team, which is true -- Waller did,&nbsp;
and she's willing to sacrifice anything and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.520
anyone to get what she wants. Did this group just&nbsp;
have bad luck, or were they always cannon fodder?

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.760
This is one question we know is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.560
to get some kind of an answer, and we've known for&nbsp;
some time. Bloodsport shot Peacemaker in the neck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.880
and left him to bleed out in the rubble. That's&nbsp;
about as certain a killshot as one can get.
 &nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.680
"Nothing like a bloodbath to start the day!"
 
Yet the post-credits scene shows Peacemaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.280
in a hospital, and Waller's underlings&nbsp;
saying that he'll help save the world.&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.080
This is all setting up for the HBO Max&nbsp;
"Peacemaker" series, so there's a near 100%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.960
chance that we'll either see or hear about his&nbsp;
rescue and survival. Even so ... a shot to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:31.840
neck is a shot to the neck. He may be a fighter,&nbsp;
but that's a hard thing to overcome -- especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:36.080
from one of Bloodsport's proprietary bullets.&nbsp;
We'll just have to wait and see on this one.&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.640
Either way, it just shows what wrestling fans&nbsp;
have known for years: John Cena never gives up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:45.360
and recovers from injury at miraculous speed.&nbsp;
Let's see if Peacemaker can win the Royal Rumble.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:47.920
"Is this thing a dog?"

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.360
Weasel is the definition of a throwaway character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.840
In fact, Weasel is several different kinds of&nbsp;
throwaway. He drowns pretty much right away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:59.920
with his meaningless death helping set the&nbsp;
movie's comic and violent sensibilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.880
But he's also a literal throwaway character,&nbsp;
as in he was thrown away, out of a helicopter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.440
But wait! A post-credits scene reveals that&nbsp;
Weasel survived! He coughs up some water and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:14.240
wanders into the woods, seemingly oblivious&nbsp;
to everything that transpired. Now what?&nbsp;

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:18.560
Seriously, though, what happens now? Will we&nbsp;
ever see Weasel again? Did Weasel get immunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.960
due to Bloodsport's deal with Waller, or was he&nbsp;
exempt since he knows nothing of the hard drive?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:27.760
Will Weasel become the Bigfoot of Corto Maltese?&nbsp;
There's so many unanswered questions here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.400
certainly enough to justify a short on HBO&nbsp;
Max -- or at least some bonkers fanfic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.720
The possibilities for more Weasel are endless.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.360
Amanda Waller is a dangerous person to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.840
associated with under any circumstances. If&nbsp;
you're her enemy, you're probably going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.480
die. If you're her ally, she could turn on you the&nbsp;
moment you're no longer useful -- at which point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.480
she doesn't care if you live or die. Even if&nbsp;
you're a loyal employee, you might end up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.240
the wrong place at the wrong time and -- as&nbsp;
her team in the first "Suicide Squad' movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:58.560
learned -- she'll probably kill you herself.
Given that she once executed her own team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.160
entirely because they accidentally ended&nbsp;
up in a mission they weren't cleared for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:07.040
it's easy to see why people fear her. As such,&nbsp;
it took an incomprehensible amount of courage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:12.000
for her team to literally knock her out and let&nbsp;
Task Force X save the day here. The question is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.800
will she let that violent insubordination stand?
The movie ends after Starro is defeated and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.760
Bloodsport makes his deal with Waller. What her&nbsp;
team knows of the deal is uncertain. What does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:25.520
matter is that they struck one of the most&nbsp;
dangerous and vindictive people on Earth in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.840
the head, and it's hard to see them getting away&nbsp;
with that. Even if she's not going to kill them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:32.720
she certainly has other ways of&nbsp;
making their lives hell -- and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:37.120
it's unlikely they'll get off scot free.
 
